   552	3) Ignored RE areas by SLR:  We concede that the
   553	classification provided in Table V is neither exhau stive nor
   554	complete, as it does not represent all the areas of  RE-related
   555	research covered in the literature. It only represe nts those RE
   556	research areas that our selected SLR has covered. F or example,
   557	goal-oriented requirements engineering, requirement s
   558	engineering in law, and requirements modeling notat ions have
   559	been the subject of many publications but not cover ed by any
   560	SLR so far. However, mapping the topics covered by the SLR
   561	against those suggested by [1, 2] for future resear ch has
   562	enabled us to identify some of the current gaps in the RE
   563	research as described above. According to the RE ro admap by
   564	Chang and Atlee [2] published in 2007, further rese arch within
   565	some ‘hotspot’ areas in RE have been suggested. The ir
   566	roadmap was published around the time when RE resea rchers
   567	started showing interest in conducting systematic r eviews.
   568	Among the identified topics by Chang and Atlee [2] for further
   569	research, the SLR in our results have addressed Security
   570	Requirements , RE education and curricula development ,
   571	Requirements Reuse , Global and Distributed RE . The SLR
   572	have not covered the topics of Requirements Scaling , RE for
   573	self-management systems , effects of system environment on RE
   574	and effectiveness of RE research in practice . Nuseibeh and
   575	Easterbrook [1] have highlighted two important area s within RE: conflict resolution among requirements  and requirements
   576	negotiation , which are not covered by any SLR so far.
   577	IV. LIMITATIONS OF THE STUDY
   578	Though we have succeeded to closely follow the sear ch
   579	strategy based on the guidelines of EBSE to ensure the
   580	completeness of our sample, but there is always a s mall risk
   581	that there would be some papers that were not inclu ded in our
   582	data collection due to their unavailability in elec tronic
   583	resources or because they may not have used the rel evant
   584	keywords in their title or abstract. To mitigate th is risk, we
   585	have attempted to triangulate our results with seco ndary
   586	searches.  Out of the 64 included papers, we were u nable to
   587	retrieve the publication details of one SLR (S40). We decided
   588	not to exclude this SLR in current results as we we re interested
   589	to know any SLR conducted in all areas of RE that i s available
   590	online. But for our future work for contributing to  the
   591	development of a new roadmap of RE we will not be
   592	considering the non peer-reviewed studies or SLR wi th low
   593	quality score in our work.
   594	To answer RQ1, we extracted the topics from the tit les and
   595	abstracts of the selected SLRs. Then the first auth or grouped
   596	the extracted topics and appropriately named each g roup as
   597	listed in Table V. Although the other two authors t hen
   598	reviewed these names given to each group and agreed  on the
   599	final names but it is possible that other researche rs may select
   600	different titles for naming each group. In our futu re analysis of
   601	the RE SLRs, we plan to provide a short description  for each
   602	group to provide further clarification of what is i ncluded in
   603	each group. For RQ2, as mentioned above, we have cl osely
   604	followed the quality assessment criteria recommende d by the
   605	EBSE guidelines. Hence the quality of our quality a ssessment
   606	is as good as what those guidelines have provided. We
   607	anticipate that in future as the EBSE community evo lves and
   608	matures, these guidelines may further be enhanced a nd
   609	improved thus increasing the confidence in the SLR quality
   610	assessment. We have also observed that the most cit ed SLR in
   611	RE, S2[A] from Davis et. al., does not show the hig hest quality
   612	score. Finally, for RQ3, we conceded that our gap a nalysis is
   613	neither complete nor exhaustive and it merely prese nts our
   614	preliminary observations. To make this a complete l ist requires
   615	deeper analysis of all selected primary studies.
   616	V. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE WORK
   617	The tertiary study reported in this paper has ident ified 53
   618	unique SLR from 64 publications in the period 2006- 2014.
   619	This paper represents the first ever tertiary study  in the RE
   620	research literature. As such we anticipate that the  data gathered
   621	and the results presented in this paper would be of  great value
   622	to future RE researchers, in particular for doctora l students to
   623	provide an effective starting point for an overview  of all the
   624	researched areas so far in RE. Furthermore, we have  been able
   625	to identify various research gaps from our mapping that is
   626	beneficial for those interested in selecting fruitf ul areas of RE
   627	research. In this paper, we have also identified so me of the
   628	anomalies in the results of already published SLR i n RE that
   629	highlight potential opportunities for SLR replicati on in the
   630
   631	--- Page 8 ---
   632	future. Almost half of the selected SLR for our stu dy have
   633	ignored to evaluate the quality of the primary stud ies included
   634	in their reviews. Careful attention should be paid to quality
   635	assessment criteria by future researchers.
   636	This study is the first step in our research plan f or
   637	contributing to an updated roadmap of RE following the
   638	roadmaps published in 2000 [5] and 2007 [4]. We are  planning
   639	to retrieve all the citations from the published SL R and create a
   640	larger repository to combine the results within all  the topics of
   641	RE in order to assess the strength of these areas f or the future
   642	generations of RE researchers. Furthermore, we woul d like to
   643	contribute to the online RE bibliography created by  Alan Davis
   644	[13] that is up to 2010 by updating the database to  include
   645	publications from 2010 to 2014  [6].
